Hooks in function.c, the bridges into make's own function table, which stays static. The
star builtin looks up the builtin it wraps, and a handle joins the table. amk's builtins
take their rows in the table. The profiler times every builtin and every call of a macro,
and a call keeps its argument count for amk.args. A function a guest defines is credited
to the engine that defined it. The engine builtins
register from the engine rows, each with a star twin. The guest handle's call runs a make
function or macro, and a guest asks whether a name is one.

